--- n=8 partial (order-7 Paley family) ---
n=8, 7+1-orbit tournaments: 2 classes with |Aut|=21, BOTH NON-SC (SC=False).
=> the Paley-extended family is NOT self-complementary at n=8; contributes 0 to #{SC & |Aut|>8}.
   The SC super-symmetric classes at n=8 come from order-3/5 auto structures (deferred; full enumeration hard).
--- MAIN RESULT ---
excess(n) = #{SC classes with |Aut|>n}, VERIFIED n=4..7 = 0,0,1,3 (matches opus/klein excess exactly).
The SC condition is ESSENTIAL: at n=7, of 5 super-symmetric (|Aut|>7) classes only 3 are SC, and excess=3
(the non-SC super-symmetric pair up under complement and do NOT force excess).
CORRECTION: my S81 formula kappa(7)=1+C(5,2)=11 is WRONG; opus/klein found kappa(7)=12 (the lazy-caterer
formula 1+C(n-2,2) BREAKS at n=7). excess(7)=kappa(7)-info-floor=12-9=3.
